Z||000001||jmw||08-10-2000||08:49 PM||||Cannot help you directly, but found site called Fiero Online Service that has trouble-shooting for various stuff, including headlights.  Don't know if any good, but it's at<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.qtm.net/~lcur/osg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.qtm.net/~lcur/osg.htm</A> <P>You have to scroll down and click on the individual topics. The headings at top appear to be broken links. Headlights apparently common problem. I know the Forum  can help you out! These guys are experts.<P>Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000002||stimpy||08-10-2000||09:07 PM||||Bad Gears! Sounds as if you have teeth broken on either end of the range of the motor. In my experience the limit switch being bad will cause te motor to move partially up or down, at any rate, its time to get different motors or rebuild the ones you got. <P>Better advice, I'm sure, will follow.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
